120..195 Comment "/// The binary corolla\'s code holds `plus`, `plus` with its inputs swapped,"
196..275 Comment "/// `times` and `times` swapped. `cross` exchanges `plus` and `times` and fixes"
276..356 Comment "/// both swapped forms: it is its own inverse, so code univalence accepts it and"
357..427 Comment "/// the hand-built product is a path, but it does not commute with the"
428..473 Comment "/// corolla\'s input swap, so `ua` refuses it."
